---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Final Stages of EPA Method 28 WHH-PTS Testing for Vedolux Boilers | Smokeless Heat Blog" description="The testing for the non-lambda boilers shows these model types will still be a viable solution even after the 2020 EPA emissions levels kick in.">
  <Header />

  <main class="pt-24">
    <section class="py-16 bg-charcoal text-cream">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
        <p class="text-ember text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-4">News</p>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl">Final Stages of EPA Method 28 WHH-PTS Testing for Vedolux Boilers</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="py-16 bg-cream">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 space-y-6 text-charcoal/90 leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          Testing for the non-lambda boilers shows that these model types will still be a viable solution even after the 2020 EPA emissions levels take effect.
        </p>

        <p>
          Now for the scores. If you compare these to the current list of cord-wood boilers on the EPA site, you will see that they score very well.
        </p>

        <p>
          The test method is Method 28 WHH-PTS. It uses real cord wood rather than cribs, and emissions are collected from the match to the end of the burn. Our boilers have always been full thermal-storage type boilers and will continue to be under the new rules. The required thermal storage is quite close to what each current manual lists as required. Updated manuals will list the minimum thermal storage values each boiler was tested with, which will now be mandated for every installation.
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-8">
          <table class="min-w-full border border-wood/30">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-wood/10">
                <th class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Model</th>
                <th class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">lb/mmBtu (weighted annual average)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2 font-medium" colspan="2">Non-Lambda</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">Vedolux 30</td>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">0.17</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">Vedolux 37</td>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">0.11</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">Vedolux 55</td>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">0.11</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2 font-medium" colspan="2">Lambda</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">Vedolux 350</td>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">0.08</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">Vedolux 450</td>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">0.04</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">Vedolux 650</td>
                <td class="border border-wood/30 px-4 py-2">0.08</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p>
          Page from the V37 test copy draft showing the values:
        </p>

        <img src="/images/v37-test-draft.png" alt="V37 test draft showing values" class="w-full border border-wood/20" />

        <p class="text-sm text-wood mt-12 pt-6 border-t border-wood/20">
          Originally published: October 2016
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
